{{Quote|JUST SAY 'I QUIT' AND THE DROID TRUCK WILL TAKE YOU BACK DOWN THE HILL! BACK TO YOUR MOMMIES AND YOUR NANNY DROIDS!|[[Lieutenant]] [[Currahee]] to a group of [[Imperial cadet]]s|<ref name="Servants of the Empire: Rebel in the Ranks">''[[Servants of the Empire: Rebel in the Ranks]]''</ref>}}
[[File:R0-Z67.png|thumb|right|270px|Nanny droid [[RO-Z67]] tending to [[Wee Dunn]], a [[Force-sensitive]] [[Rodian]] child, on [[Mustafar]].]]
'''Nanny droids''',<ref name="Children of the Force">{{TCW|Children of the Force}}</ref> also known as '''Nurse droids''',<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref> '''childcare droids''',<ref name="Mission to Disaster">''[[The High Republic: Mission to Disaster]]''</ref> or a '''child care droid''',<ref name="A Valiant Vow">''[[The High Republic: A Valiant Vow]]''</ref> were a model of [[droid]]s designed to care for the young, though they could also function as nurses.<ref name="Conspiracy">{{TCW|Conspiracy}}</ref><ref name="Voices">{{TCW|Voices}}</ref> The [[RO-series childcare and nanny droid]] had a multitude of [[Limb|appendages]] that folded into their body<ref name="Children of the Force" /> and two [[Foodstuff|food]] storage tanks were attached to their upper torso.<ref name="Episode Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/children-of-the-force-episode-guide|text="Children of the Force" Episode Guide - The Clone Wars}}</ref> The [[Imperial nanny droid]]s also functioned as [[medical droid]]s.<ref name="Eminence">{{TCW|Eminence (episode)}}</ref> Movement was facilitated through a wheeled locomotion unit. [[Auntie Nags]] was a nanny droid.<ref name="Edge of the Galaxy">''[[Servants of the Empire: Edge of the Galaxy]]''</ref> Youth tended to outgrow nanny droids quickly and, for this reason, [[Ghirra Starros]] considered them a waste of [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]].<ref name="A Test of Courage">''[[The High Republic: A Test of Courage]]''</ref>

[[IG-series]] [[assassin droid]] [[IG-11]] was reprogrammed and converted into a nanny droid by the [[Ugnaught]] [[Kuiil]], initially made to serve as a helping hand before he ultimately served as nurse droid to [[Din Grogu|Grogu]].<ref name="Chapter7">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 7: The Reckoning}}</ref> [[WA-2V]] was the nanny droid of [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] of [[Alderaan]].<ref name="Princess and Scoundrel">''[[The Princess and the Scoundrel]]''</ref>

[[Aryssha Starros|Aryssha]] had a childcare droid aboard ''[[King's Ransom]]'' to assist her during her pregnancy. She [[Slicer|sliced]] it and used it to disable the ship's [[hyperdrive]] so that her [[Starros Clan|family]] could [[Capture of the King's Ransom|rescue]] her.<ref name="Sana Starros 5">[[Sana Starros 5|''Sana Starros'' 5]]</ref>

